-- title:
--   Local triviality at a crossing of a degree-zero divisorial sheaf
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a package $\mathfrak{X}$ of Deligne–Rapoport model data for $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $\varpi$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ with a ring map $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$, and a resolved-model package $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}$ over these data, with total space $Y$, structure map $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}$ to the base change of the Deligne–Rapoport model along $\mathbb{Z} \to O$, node set with widths, and component ideal sheaves $\mathrm{comp}(v)$ indexed by $v \in \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \oplus \Sigma_{nd}\mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(nd)-1)$. Let $Fc$ assign to each $e$ a family $(Fc\,e\,k)_{k \in \mathrm{Fin}(e+1)}$ of ideal sheaf data on the resolution $\mathrm{Resolution}\,\varpi\,e$ of $uv = \varpi^{e}$, such that on each standard chart $\mathrm{Resolution}.\iota\,\varpi\,e\,i$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,e$) the pullback of $Fc\,e\,k$ is the ideal sheaf attached to $(V\varpi)$ if $k = i$, to $(U\varpi)$ if $k = i+1$, and to the unit ideal otherwise; let $ch$ be étale crossing-chart data for $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}$, $\varpi$ and $Fc$, providing in particular open sets $ch.U\,n$ around the crossing points. Let $\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_m$ be sections of $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,O$, with exponents $\mathrm{pos}_j, \mathrm{neg}_j \in \mathbb{N}$ and assigned components $v_j$, such that the image of the closed point of $O$ under $\sigma_j$ lies in the locus $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{smoothOffEdges}$, lies in the support of $\mathrm{comp}(v_j)$, and lies in the support of no other $\mathrm{comp}(w)$. Let $a^{+}, a^{-}$ be natural-number-valued functions on the component index set satisfying, for every node $nd$ and every $i \in \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(nd)-1)$, the vanishing $\sum_{j} [v_j = \mathrm{inr}\langle nd,i\rangle](\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j) + \alpha(a^{+}-a^{-})(\mathrm{inr}\langle nd,i\rangle) = 0$, where $\alpha$ is the intersection map $c \mapsto (j \mapsto \sum_i c_i \cdot \mathrm{inter}(i,j))$ of the component table $\mathrm{x0MqResolvedTable}$ of the widths. Then for every node $n$ there is an open $V$ of the base-changed Deligne–Rapoport model containing the crossing point of $n$ and contained in $ch.U\,n$, such that the pullback along the inclusion of $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}^{-1}V$ of the module $\bigotimes_j \bigl((\ker \sigma_j)^{\mathrm{pos}_j}\bigr)^{\vee} \otimes (\ker \sigma_j)^{\mathrm{neg}_j} \otimes \bigl(\prod_F \mathrm{comp}(F)^{a^{+}_F}\bigr)^{\vee} \otimes \prod_F \mathrm{comp}(F)^{a^{-}_F}$ — formed by folding over $\mathrm{List.finRange}\,m$, each ideal sheaf contributing its associated module and dual module — is isomorphic to the unit sheaf of modules on $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}^{-1}V$.
--
--   This is the local, per-crossing step of the descent of divisorial sheaves along the resolution $Y \to \mathfrak{X}_O$: the numerical condition on exceptional components forces the twisted sheaf to be trivial on the preimage of a neighbourhood of each crossing point. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_isInvertible_and_pullback_toDR_iso_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_isInvertible_and_pullback_toDR_iso_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero), which glues these local trivialisations with the isomorphism over the smooth locus to obtain an invertible module on the Deligne–Rapoport model whose pullback is the given twisted sheaf.
